ADUC is the administrative software window that system administrators use every day. It looks like a file explorer tree showing:

The Builtin folder: Standard administrative groups.

The Computers folder: Where any newly added laptop automatically lands.

The Domain Controllers folder: Where the primary identity servers live.

Organizational Units (OUs): The departments (IT, Sales, HR).

Resetting Passwords: When an employee forgets their password on Monday morning, the IT Helpdesk opens this tool, right-clicks the user, and clicks "Reset Password".
